#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105485 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105910 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "796da155-1e8c-5f6c-896f-2dce9a678f5b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Expressions with Binomial Terms"}] :question/id #uuid "45b1ee7d-b7ce-5336-9d2a-1a5953310026" :question/math-academy-id "e-1521" :question/problem "Find an expression equivalent to $\\dfrac 27\\, {(y-3)}$" :question/worked-solution "Writing $y-3$ as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{y-3}{1}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2}{7}(y - 3) &= \\frac{2}{7} \\cdot (y - 3) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{7} \\cdot \\frac{y - 3}{1} \\\\\n&= (2 \\cdot (y - 3))/(7 \\cdot 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2y - 6}{7}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105486 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105911 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afca9dea-4471-582f-b15f-a5899d3789aa" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Expressions with Positive Terms"}] :question/id #uuid "53825e9f-1b2f-582e-ad91-50970995d523" :question/math-academy-id "e-1543" :question/problem "Find an expression that's equivalent to $\\dfrac{2}3 a$." :question/worked-solution "Writing $a$ as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{a}{1}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2}{3}a &= \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{a}{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 \\cdot a}{3 \\cdot 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2a}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the expressions\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{3}a\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2a}{3}\n$$\n\nare equivalent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105487 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105912 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7002c6fc-ae50-5b7f-995f-2147db19e9ec" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Fraction as a Product"}] :question/id #uuid "0c24fff9-3d43-53f3-8c87-daacb675f802" :question/math-academy-id "e-1544" :question/problem "Find an expression equivalent to $\\dfrac{2(3-x)}{5}$." :question/worked-solution "Pulling out the variable part, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(2(3 - x))/(5) &= (2 \\cdot (3 - x))/(5 \\cdot 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{5} \\cdot \\frac{3 - x}{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{5} \\cdot (3 - x) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{5}(3 - x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105683 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd86e42a-deb3-5f59-bbbc-f096a1f368aa" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Expressions with Negative Terms"}] :question/id #uuid "9062b933-10d8-5f52-b41e-c528d35c9fe5" :question/math-academy-id "e-832" :question/problem "Find an expression equivalent to $-\\dfrac{2}9 (-z)$." :question/worked-solution "First, remember that the product of two negative numbers is a positive number. Thus,\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{2}9 (-z) = \\dfrac{2}{9} z\n$$\n\nNow, writing $z$ as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{z}{1}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2}{9}z &= \\frac{2}{9} \\cdot z \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{9} \\cdot \\frac{z}{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 \\cdot z}{9 \\cdot 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2z}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the expressions\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{2}9 (-z)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2z}{9}\n$$\n\nare equivalent."}]}
